     restore runs automatically before services start)

  Phase 2 — when you have 100k MON ready, PROMOTE to validator:
    sudo ./monad-validator-setup --network=testnet --validator \
      --beneficiary=0x<YOUR_REAL_REWARDS_ADDRESS> \
      --node-name=<UNIQUE_MONIKER> \
      --generate-keys --keys-password=auto
    (re-running detects full→validator transition; backs up the existing
     full-node node.toml, swaps in the validator template, patches the
     beneficiary, generates keys, signs name-record)

  After Phase 2: addValidator() on-chain via staking-sdk-cli + 100k MON
  self-stake (see github.com/monad-developers/staking-sdk-cli).

FULL AUTOMATION (zero prompts — CI / re-installs)
  sudo ./monad-validator-setup --non-interactive \
    --network=testnet \
    --triedb-partition=nvme1n1 --allow-nvme-reformat \
    --beneficiary=0x<YOUR_REWARDS_ADDRESS> \
    --node-name=<UNIQUE_MONIKER> \
    --generate-keys --keys-password=auto \
    --snapshot-restore --start-services

OPERATOR INPUT NEEDED (cannot be auto-detected)
